 "description":
 "A negative condition declares n, and so does the match after it, which is a reuse WellFormed allows. A delete arrives. These inverses keep the specification's nesting, so each n stays in its own scope. jinaga.js's invertSpecification re-roots: its inverse for the match n binds n first and then declares n again inside the event's condition, where n is in scope (Inverse.lean, checked by lake exe vectors)."}
